From ef08ef9d3f9c672bc7ff47f4bce37fb789ded0c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusheng Su <yushengsu.thu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:52:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Feat] dflash: Serve MoE FFN drafts from the config's HF MoE
 fields

SpecForge trains DFlash-family drafts (DFlash, DFlash2, DSpark) whose FFN
is a mixture of experts; the export stacks the experts as
experts.gate_up_proj [E, 2I, H] / experts.down_proj [E, H, I] and may ship
a trained router bias (gate.expert_bias). SGLang's draft classes only built
the dense DFlashMLP and dropped the expert tensors silently, serving an
uninitialized FFN.

The decoder layer now builds its FFN through build_dflash_ffn: DFlashMoE
when the config has routed experts, the dense MLP otherwise, so every
existing class (DFlashDraftModel, DFlash2DraftModel, Qwen3DSparkModel, ...)
serves both. DFlashMoE is driven by the HF MoE fields the Qwen, DeepSeek
and Mixtral families share, not by a model family: SGLang's TopK for the
routing the config describes (softmax or sigmoid scores, renormalization,
group-limited top-k, routed scaling), FusedMoE for the experts, Qwen2MoeMLP
as a gated (Qwen) or summed (DeepSeek) shared expert. The router bias is
the checkpoint's call: gate.expert_bias or gate.e_score_correction_bias is
applied when present (biased softmax top-k runs in torch, since the fused
softmax routers keep softmax routing bias-free), absent means the unbiased
top-k. Loading accepts the stacked and the per-expert expert names and both
shared-expert names, and is strict: MoE tensors aimed at a dense layer and
partially loaded FFNs are refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
